2. How will you control the log files?

Since logs are continuously increasing, so we need to use log rotation.

example:
                    Log file
                        ↓
                  Reaches limit
                        ↓
                Old log → compressed
                        ↓
              New log file created
                        ↓
           Old logs deleted after some time

Conclusion: Proper partitioning and log rotation keep disk space under control, prevent logs from exceeding 10 GB, and ensure critical services run without interruption.


