      improving Linux CPU performance using kernel-level techniques.

          * Scheduler tuning – control how the CPU gives time to different processes.
          * Process priority – use nice / renice to give important processes higher priority.
          * Real-time scheduling – use chrt for time-critical processes.
          * CPU affinity – use taskset to assign a process to specific CPU cores.
          * Kernel modules – load only the required modules to avoid unnecessary overhead.

